    "body": "### Problem\n\nMulticursor with enabled follow mode doesn't update extra cursors with active Visual mode in some situations with custom mappings.\n\nMight be the same root cause as in #41606.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. Create the following `init.lua`:\n\n    ```lua\n    -- Setting/updating already active visual selection\n    _G.triselect = function()\n      local cursor = vim.api.nvim_win_get_cursor(0)\n      vim.api.nvim_win_set_cursor(0, { cursor[1], cursor[2] + 1 })\n      vim.cmd('normal! o')\n      vim.api.nvim_win_set_cursor(0, { cursor[1], cursor[2] + 3 })\n    end\n    vim.keymap.set('x', 'gh', '<Cmd>lua _G.triselect()<CR>')\n\n    -- Stopping and re-selecting\n    _G.slideselect = function()\n      vim.cmd('normal! \"_y')\n      vim.cmd('normal! 2l')\n      vim.cmd('normal! 1v')\n    end\n    vim.keymap.set('x', 'gl', '<Cmd>lua _G.slideselect()<CR>')\n\n    -- Start Visual mode from Normal mode\n    _G.initselect = function()\n      local cursor = vim.api.nvim_win_get_cursor(0)\n      vim.cmd('normal! v')\n      vim.api.nvim_win_set_cursor(0, { cursor[1], cursor[2] + 2 })\n\n      -- Although doing just this works\n      -- vim.cmd('normal! vlll')\n    end\n    vim.keymap.set('n', 'gL', '<Cmd>lua _G.initselect()<CR>')\n\n    -- Pre-populate text for easier repro\n    vim.api.nvim_buf_set_lines(0, 0, -1, false, { 'aaaaaaa', 'bbbbbbb', 'ccccccc' })\n    vim.bo.modified = false\n    ```\n\n2. `nvim --clean -u init.lua`\n3. Type `vip` - `Q` to start multicursor with follow mode enabled.\n4. Do one of the following:\n    4.1. `v` - `gh`. The main cursor expands the selected region to the right, but extra cursors don't.\n    4.2. `vl` to create a two cell visual selection at all cursors; `gl`. The main cursor Visual selection is \"moved\", but all previous cursors are not updated (including what was the selection of the main cursor).\n    4.3. `gL`. The main cursor has three cell visual selection, while extra cursors don't *and* the previous position for main cursor is not updated.\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nExtra cursor always follow the main cursor if follow mode is enabled. In particular, when Visual mode is involved: selection is updated, selection is stopped and re-created somewhere else, selection is initiated.\n\n### Nvim version (nvim -v)\n\nNVIM v0.13.0-dev-1658+gd1fd8158de\n\n### Vim (not Nvim) behaves the same?\n\nNo, doesn't have this functionality\n\n### Operating system/version\n\nEndeavourOS Linux x86_64, 7.2.4-arch1-2\n\n### Terminal name/version\n\nGhostty 1.3.1-arch2\n\n### $TERM environment variable\n\nxterm-ghostty\n\n### Installation\n\nAppimage and from source",
